---
import CodeExample from '@/components/CodeExample.astro'
import ComponentLayout from '@/layouts/ComponentLayout.astro'
import { buildUrl } from '@/scripts/constants'
---

<ComponentLayout name='Ajax HTML'>
	<p>
		<code>tui-ajax-html</code> renders an HTML response from the shared query cache. Use a stable
		query key to connect it to an <code>ajax-fetch</code> search or an <code>ajax-form</code>
		submission. Those explicit user actions take precedence over this component's initial fetch; the
		URL here is for loading HTML when no newer cached result exists.
	</p>
	<h2>Lazy results with shared controls</h2>
	<p>
		The form and results use the same key. The HTML request starts near the viewport only if
		another component has not already populated the cache. Responses may contain an element
		matching this component's ID, or a body whose content should be inserted directly.
	</p>
	<CodeExample>
		<tui-ajax-fetch data-tui-query-key='shared-messages' data-tui-announce-id='messages-status'>
			<form method='GET' action={buildUrl('/api/messages')}>
				<div class='form-group'>
					<label for='messages-query'>Search</label>
					<input id='messages-query' type='search' name='query' />
				</div>
				<button type='submit'>Search</button>
			</form>
		</tui-ajax-fetch>
		<div id='messages-status' role='status' class='visually-hidden'>
			<span data-tui-announce-title></span>
		</div>
		<tui-ajax-html
			class='block'
			id='messages-results'
			data-tui-query-key='shared-messages'
			data-tui-url={buildUrl('/api/messages')}
			data-tui-load-strategy='lazy'
		>
			<p>Search to load messages.</p>
		</tui-ajax-html>
	</CodeExample>

	<h2>Choose a load strategy</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>initial</code>: fetch as soon as the component initializes.</li>
		<li><code>lazy</code>: fetch when the component approaches the viewport.</li>
		<li><code>defer</code>: wait until <code>DOMContentLoaded</code>.</li>
		<li>
			<code>server-side</code>: do not fetch; use server-rendered markup and cache updates.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		If the cache already contains data when a lazy load is due, that data renders without
		another request. If a fetch or form response arrives while the lazy request is in flight,
		the newer shared-cache result remains visible.
	</p>

	<h2>Share results with a form</h2>
	<p>
		Mutations can use the same key. A successful form response replaces the cached HTML
		immediately, while the <code>ajax-html</code> URL remains a fallback for its initial lazy load.
	</p>
	<CodeExample>
		<tui-ajax-form
			data-tui-query-key='shared-messages'
			data-tui-announce-id='message-submit-status'
		>
			<form method='POST' action={buildUrl('/api/messages')}>
				<label for='new-message'>New message</label>
				<textarea id='new-message' name='message' required></textarea>
				<button type='submit'>Post</button>
			</form>
			<div id='message-submit-status' role='status' class='visually-hidden'>
				<span data-tui-announce-title></span>
			</div>
		</tui-ajax-form>
	</CodeExample>
</ComponentLayout>
